                <pb facs="0385" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72113/1141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Guatemala</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-22T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 22,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your November 11, 8 p.m. and November 3, 4 p.m. Department cannot understand why
                    the addresserdo [<hi rendition="#italic">acuerdo</hi>] referred to in your
                    telegrams of November 11, 8 p.m., and November <pb facs="0386" n="301"
                        xml:id="pg301"/> 3, 4 p.m., has not been published. The Department thinks
                    that it should be published at the earliest moment and desires to be informed of
                    the date when it will be published. You are instructed to bring this matter
                    again to the attention of the Guatemalan Government and to impress upon it the
                    importance with which the Department regards this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
